    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the others are base/helper classes), and the full `mvnw test` build passed with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the normalized telephone is already used by another owner, returning **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the colliding normalized telephone, following the pattern of the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after normalizing the telephone (existing 10-digit strip logic), it now calls a new `rejectDuplicateTelephone(...)` helper before saving. The helper strips non-digits from each existing owner's stored telephone and compares against the new normalized value, so numbers that differ only in formatting still collide. On a match it throws `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException`.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` that returns `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` (409) with a `ProblemDetail` body carrying `errors: [\"telephone\"]`, consistent with the shape used by the other handlers.\n\nTest results: `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone` (expects 409 on a duplicate) and `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone` (expects 2xx for distinct numbers) both pass; `BUILD SUCCESS` for the full suite.",
